      "verdict": "REFUTED, and the refutation was paid for. C7 over-estimates d32 by a factor above 2, so the seam-subtraction bias was never the source of its d32 relative error and growing the caps back could not fix it by that mechanism. The mode was adopted anyway, on Meyer 1994 and on mask quality, and d32 relative error duly got WORSE. That cost is stated in the constant ledger, in the engine docstring and in verification/phase1-adoption.json."
